🔴 P0 — Launch-blocking
BUG-1: Module completion / XP / BROski$ does not persist
Severity: Critical — breaks the core product loop
Repro steps:

Sign in, go to /courses/designing-your-focus-zone (M1)

Answer all 5 quiz questions correctly → UI shows "Score: 4/4 (100%)" live, before submitting

Click "Submit Quiz"

Click "✅ Mark as Complete" (button becomes enabled/purple, click registers)

Check top nav XP bar, /courses, /profile, /pets

Expected: XP +30, BROski$ +10, M1 marked complete, module progress ticks to 1/12
Actual:

Top nav XP bar stays at 0 / 1,000

BROski$ balance stays at 0

/courses module progress stays 0/12, M1 card still shows "Start quest →"

/profile still shows 0 Courses, 0 Badges

/pets "Recent Activity" still shows placeholder "Your first XP lands here"

Likely cause: Mark as Complete write either isn't hitting Supabase, isn't awaited before UI reads stale cache, or the read-side query isn't refetching after mutation. Worth checking RLS on the write path too, given the recent is_admin() / 42501 history — same "authenticated user can't write/read their own row" pattern could be at play here.
Suggested fix: Trace the Mark as Complete handler end to end — confirm the Supabase insert/update actually commits (check table directly), then confirm the frontend refetches XP/BROski$/profile state after a successful write rather than relying on cached client state.

BUG-2: /admin/mission-control force-signs the user out instead of denying access
Severity: Critical — security/session integrity issue
Repro steps:

While signed in, navigate to /admin/mission-control

Page shows "Checking access..." briefly

Reproduced twice, consistent

Expected: A proper 403/"not authorized" state, session untouched
Actual: Session is destroyed; user lands fully signed out on the homepage
Extra concern: This route is linked from every page's footer — the word "weird" in "Keep it weird, keep it Welsh" hyperlinks straight to /admin/mission-control. So any curious visitor clicking that footer word gets booted out of their own session.
Suggested fix:

Fix the access-check to return an in-place "access denied" UI, not a sign-out.

Remove the /admin/mission-control link from the public footer entirely, or gate the link's visibility to admins only.

🟡 P1 — User-facing broken feature
BUG-3: Referral button is non-functional
Severity: High — visible dead CTA
Repro steps: Go to /tokens, click "Refer a friend — earn 100 BROski$"
Actual: Nothing happens. DevTools shows an INP warning: "Event handlers on this element blocked UI updates for 202.2ms." No link generated, no copy action, no error shown to user.
Note: This matches the already-known open issue — get_or_create_referral_code() is missing a safe EXECUTE grant (403 for all users). Flagging here because it's a live, clickable, user-facing dead button right now, not just a backend symptom.
Suggested fix: Ship the already-scoped fix — validate p_user_id = auth.uid() internally (or drop the parameter) before granting EXECUTE — then add a proper error toast for future failures instead of a silent no-op.

